{"abstract":"Establishing digital twins is a non-trivial endeavor especially when users face significant challenges in creating them from scratch. Ready availability of re-usable models, data, functions, and tool assets, can help with creation and use of digital twins. A number of frameworks/platforms exist to facilitate creation and use of digital twins. In this paper, we propose such a platform to manage digital twin assets, create composable digital twins from re-usable assets and make the digital twins available as a service to other users. The proposed platform supports the management of re-usable assets, storage, provision of compute infrastructure, communication, monitoring, and execution tasks. Two case studies are used to demonstrate the capabilities of this platform.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Talasila, Prasad","Gomes, Cláudio","Vosteen, Lars B.","Iven, Hannes","Leucker, Martin","Gil, Santiago","Mikkelsen, Peter Høgh","Kamburjan, Eduard","Larsen, Peter Gorm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-796475"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Talasila, Prasad"],"country":["Germany","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lübeck","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Automation","Composition","Configuration","Digital twin","Life cycle","Physical twin","Platform","Reuse","Service"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"composable digital twins on digital twin as a service platform","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105001563698","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-796475","identifier":[{"id":"105001563698","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85211131840","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7bb7ac01-69a7-4549-808a-87595bd270c5"],"keyword":["Digital twin","automation","composable DTs","composition","configuration","firefighter DT","life cycle","physical twin","platform","reuse","service"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-58EDFEC32989EDF70C8CDBE21D6B25BE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Software Engineering & Computing systems - Edison"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of lübeck","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lübeck","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Prasad","key":"talasilapau","last":"Talasila","locid":"7a6e2389-0e8e-4040-8125-6fcbea9ef434","name":"Talasila, Prasad","orcid":"0000-0002-8973-2640","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cláudio","key":"gomespau","last":"Gomes","locid":"63d3d37d-ef61-40b6-a263-52792c5fd9e0","name":"Gomes, Cláudio","orcid":"0000-0003-2692-9742","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars B.","key":"vosteenpau","last":"Vosteen","name":"Vosteen, Lars B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hannes","key":"ivenpau","last":"Iven","name":"Iven, Hannes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"leuckerpau","last":"Leucker","name":"Leucker, Martin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Santiago","key":"gilpau","last":"Gil","name":"Gil, Santiago","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter H.","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"5955bc36-1ce2-45aa-b679-c2b17be56f8e","name":"Mikkelsen, Peter Høgh","name_org":"Mikkelsen, Peter H.","orcid":"0000-0003-2321-758X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eduard","key":"kamburjanpau","last":"Kamburjan","name":"Kamburjan, Eduard","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter G.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"318d787b-3528-4a49-88be-60491de69409","name":"Larsen, Peter Gorm","name_org":"Larsen, Peter G.","orcid":"0000-0002-4589-1500","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/00375497241298653","issn":["00375497","17413133"],"issn_org":["00375497"],"issue":"3","journal":"Simulation","pages":"287-311","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Simulation","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001563698","2-s2.0-85211131840"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7bb7ac01-69a7-4549-808a-87595bd270c5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Composable digital twins on Digital Twin as a Service platform","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-796475","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Co-simulation, essential for various domains, involves simulating systems with heterogeneous subsystems by combining them into scenarios using orchestration algorithms. Due to system evolutions, digital twins may require dynamic reconfiguration of the scenario and orchestration algorithm, which may introduce a significant simulation error that may go unnoticed if the scenario and orchestration algorithm are not correctly aligned. This paper introduces a monitor-based approach to automatically detect and help prevent any discrepancies between the scenario and the orchestration algorithm. The approach’s overhead may be significant for short simulations, but amortizes over longer simulations, as illustrated by a case study.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Simon Thrane","Kamburjan, Eduard","Kazemi, Zahra"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-807345"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-31","place":"Crete, gr","start":"2024-10-27","title":"12th International Symposium on Leveraging Applications of Formal Methods, Verification and Validation, ISoLA 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kamburjan, Eduard"],"country":["Luxembourg","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Luxembourg","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monitoring reconfigurable simulation scenarios in co simulated digital twins","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105003226095","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-807345","identifier":[{"id":"105003226095","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b8062a2b-272d-4ea8-a38e-4b81bbb0d2c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5F96364ECF2D250630FC5D34E85458C4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"lu","key":"university of luxembourg","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Luxembourg","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Software Engineering & Computing systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon Thrane","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Simon Thrane","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eduard","key":"kamburjanpau","last":"Kamburjan","name":"Kamburjan, Eduard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Zahra","key":"kazemipau","last":"Kazemi","locid":"89f1dfd1-04c0-41d6-8cc3-3f0b3a08192c","name":"Kazemi, Zahra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tiziana","key":"margariapedh","last":"Margaria","name":"Margaria, Tiziana","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bernhard","key":"steffenpedh","last":"Steffen","name":"Steffen, Bernhard","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-75390-9_4","isbn":["9783031753794"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"47-61","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Leveraging Applications of Formal Methods, Verification and Validation. Specification and Verification - 12th International Symposium, ISoLA 2024, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003226095"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b8062a2b-272d-4ea8-a38e-4b81bbb0d2c8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Monitoring Reconfigurable Simulation Scenarios in Co-simulated Digital Twins","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-807345","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The systematic engineering of Digital Twins (DTs) requires the establishment of clear methodologies supported by intelligent tooling. We propose an approach to guide the user in the creation and deployment of services for DTs utilizing ontologies and workflows. In our approach, the user selects a desired DT service from an array of options. This selection is then used to suggest a) enablers and models to place in the DT, and b) development and deployment workflows for the DT service. The aim is to provide DT engineering guidance to assist non-software engineering experts to develop DT services more rapidly with less effort. We describe our initial work on applying this approach to a derived version of an industrial wind turbine generator case study, utilizing openCAESAR for ontology definition and enacting the workflows with Jupyter notebooks.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Oakes, Bentley","Gomes, Cláudio","Abbiati, Giuseppe","Kamburjan, Eduard","Bas, Elif Ecem","Engelsgaard, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-787823"],"event":{"end":"2024-09-27","place":"Linz, at","start":"2024-09-22","title":"27th International Conference on Model Driven Engineering Languages and Systems, MODELS Companion 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnique Montreal","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Digital twins","Ontologies","Recommendation","Workflows"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["LORC - Fonden Lindoe Offshore Renewables Center"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards ontological service driven engineering of digital twins","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3652620.3688261","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-787823","identifier":[{"id":"85212198557","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b946a10e-4bc7-4a5d-9530-daf8ddc9f260"],"keyword":["DT services","digital twins","guided software engineering","ontologies","recommendation","wind turbine testing","workflows"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24F709C665A59DAF698F4D6FE5DC2CDB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3652620.3688261","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"polytechnique montreal","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnique Montreal","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Software Engineering & Computing systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["R&D Test Systems A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["LORC - Fonden Lindoe Offshore Renewables Center"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bentley","key":"oakespau","last":"Oakes","name":"Oakes, Bentley","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claudio","key":"gomespau","last":"Gomes","locid":"63d3d37d-ef61-40b6-a263-52792c5fd9e0","name":"Gomes, Cláudio","name_org":"Gomes, Claudio","orcid":"0000-0003-2692-9742","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Giuseppe","key":"abbiatipau","last":"Abbiati","locid":"4daeda21-5dcc-4e7b-b9bf-d2a4246dd4b6","name":"Abbiati, Giuseppe","orcid":"0000-0002-5048-8505","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eduard","key":"kamburjanpau","last":"Kamburjan","name":"Kamburjan, Eduard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Elif Ecem","key":"baspau","last":"Bas","name":"Bas, Elif Ecem","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"engelsgaardpau","last":"Engelsgaard","name":"Engelsgaard, Sebastian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3652620.3688261","eisbn":["9798400706226"],"pages":"464-469","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","status":"p","subtitle":"MODELS 2024 - ACM/IEEE 27th International Conference on Model Driven Engineering Languages and Systems: Companion Proceedings","title":"Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212198557"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","r&d test systems a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b946a10e-4bc7-4a5d-9530-daf8ddc9f260"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Towards Ontological Service-Driven Engineering of Digital Twins","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://