{"abstract":"Whereas the semantics of probabilistic languages has been extensively studied, specification languages for their properties have received less attention---with the notable exception of recent and on-going efforts by Joost-Pieter Katoen and collaborators. In this paper, we revisit probabilistic dynamic logic (pDL), a specification logic for programs in the probabilistic guarded command language (pGCL) of McIver and Morgan. Building on dynamic logic, pDL can express both first-order state properties and probabilistic reachability properties. In this paper, we report on work in progress towards a deductive proof system for pDL. This proof system, in line with verification systems for dynamic logic such as KeY, is based on forward reasoning by means of symbolic execution.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Johnsen, Einar Broch","Kamburjan, Eduard","Pardo, Raúl","Voogd, Erik","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789552"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Deductive verification","Dynamic logic","Probabilistic programs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a proof system for probabilistic dynamic logic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.00906","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-789552","identifier":[{"id":"85212131535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-60b7772c-cc33-47e0-86c8-3e09c609153f"],"keyword":["Deductive verification","Dynamic logic","Probabilistic programs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-